_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Potential null pointer dereference on authorization.**

If a connection's `authorization` is not set (e.g., connection established before this PR or during error scenarios), `$authorization` will be null. Line 659 will then throw when calling `$authorization->skip(...)`.

Consider adding a null check or fallback:
```diff
 // Get authorization from connection (stored during onOpen)
 $authorization = $realtime->connections[$connection]['authorization'] ?? null;

+if ($authorization === null) {
+    throw new Exception(Exception::GENERAL_UNAUTHORIZED_SCOPE, 'Connection authorization not found');
+}
+
 $database = getConsoleDB();
 $database->setAuthorization($authorization);
```

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
        $projectId = $realtime->connections[$connection]['projectId'] ?? null;

        // Get authorization from connection (stored during onOpen)
        $authorization = $realtime->connections[$connection]['authorization'] ?? null;

        if ($authorization === null) {
            throw new Exception(Exception::GENERAL_UNAUTHORIZED_SCOPE, 'Connection authorization not found');
        }

        $database = getConsoleDB();
        $database->setAuthorization($authorization);

        if ($projectId !== 'console') {
            $project = $authorization->skip(fn () => $database->getDocument('projects', $projectId));

            $database = getProjectDB($project);
            $database->setAuthorization($authorization);
        } else {
            $project = null;
        }
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In app/realtime.php around lines 650 to 665, the code calls
$authorization->skip(...) without verifying $authorization is non-null which can
cause a null pointer; add a guard so you check if $authorization is null before
using it and handle both cases explicitly (for example: if $authorization is
present use $authorization->skip(fn()=> $database->getDocument(...)), otherwise
either call $database->getDocument(...) directly if unauthenticated reads are
allowed or abort/return an authorization error/result), and ensure
$database->setAuthorization is only called with a valid authorization object or
skipped when null.
```

</details>

